{"ref":"BDB, קְרִי","hw":"קְרִי","html":"† <big>[<span dir=\"rtl\">קְרִי</span>]</big>  <strong>n.</strong>[<strong>m.</strong>] <strong>opposition, contrariness</strong>;—only <span dir=\"rtl\">(בְּ)קֶ֑רִי</span> in <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 26\" href=\"/Leviticus.26\">Lv 26</a>, as adv. modifier of <span dir=\"rtl\">הָלַךְ</span> (in fig. sense), + <span dir=\"rtl\">עִם</span> pers., of Isr.’s relation to <span dir=\"rtl\">י׳</span>: <span dir=\"rtl\">תֵּלְכוּ עִמִּי קֶ֑רִי</span> <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 26:21\" href=\"/Leviticus.26.21\">Lv 26:21</a> <em>if ye walk with me contrariwise</em>, so v <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 26:23\" href=\"/Leviticus.26.23\">23</a>, <span dir=\"rtl\">בְּקֶ֑רִי</span> v <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 26:27\" href=\"/Leviticus.26.27\">27</a>, <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 26:40\" href=\"/Leviticus.26.40\">40</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">י׳</span> subj., <span dir=\"rtl\">וְהָלַכְתִּי עִמָּכֶם בַּקֶּ֑רִי</span> v <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 26:24\" href=\"/Leviticus.26.24\">24</a>, so v <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 26:41\" href=\"/Leviticus.26.41\">41</a> and (<span dir=\"rtl\">בַּחֲמַת ק׳</span> <em>in wrath of opposition</em>) v <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 26:28\" href=\"/Leviticus.26.28\">28</a>.","next":"BDB, מִקְרֶה²","prev":"BDB, קָרֶה"}